  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened National Preparedness, Response and Resilience to COVID19 in Cambodia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In collaboration with UN partners, under the UN MPTF for COVD-19 Response, this joint programme will strengthen the access to COVID-19 information, prevention, and mitigation for returning migrants to prevent a large scale community transmission in the host communities. Secondly, the programme will improve access to essential health and social services for returning migrants upon crossing the border, to quarantine facilities for 14 days given the need to access essential health services for the most vulnerable returning migrants and a follow up for support to services to the most vulnerable migrants upon their return, which includes host communities&apos; access to continued essential health services provided by community health workers, primary health care staff at the Rural Health Center and support from village/commune leaders.</narrative>
  </description>
